  "statement_token": "\"Let $D$ be a reduced alternating diagram of a knot $K$ with determinant $p$, where $p$ is prime. A **Fox $p$-coloring** is a coloring of the arcs of $D$ by elements of $\\\\mathbb Z_p$ satisfying the crossing relations, and it is non-trivial when not all arcs receive the same color. **Kauffman–Harary conjecture.** Every non-trivial $p$-coloring of $D$ assigns different colors to different arcs.\\n\\nThe conjecture was proved in full generality by Mattman and Solis using pseudo-colorings, so it is no longer open.\"",
  "statement_token_sha256": "79ee062843bc76cafbafed1dc87ad19812dd86c1e36264ab42f0c41b8852a5ba",
  "statement": "Let $D$ be a reduced alternating diagram of a knot $K$ with determinant $p$, where $p$ is prime. A **Fox $p$-coloring** is a coloring of the arcs of $D$ by elements of $\\mathbb Z_p$ satisfying the crossing relations, and it is non-trivial when not all arcs receive the same color. **Kauffman–Harary conjecture.** Every non-trivial $p$-coloring of $D$ assigns different colors to different arcs.\n\nThe conjecture was proved in full generality by Mattman and Solis using pseudo-colorings, so it is no longer open.",
